Xmahjongg 3.7 for Helios
==========================

Start /helios/bin/x11/xmahjongg, or choose Play -> Mahjong solitaire.
The command xshanghai is an alias for the same game.

Remove matching pairs of free tiles: a free tile has no tile above it and
at least one open side. Flowers match other flowers; seasons match seasons.

Controls: h hints, Return takes a hinted match, u undoes, r redoes,
n starts a new game, c cleans up, s solves, Escape cancels, q quits.
Arrow keys and Space also allow keyboard play.

Use --number 42 for a repeatable board; --list lists the available layouts,
tilesets and backgrounds. Select them with --layout and --tileset.
The --tileset small option is useful on smaller displays.
Data files live in /helios/local/share/xmahjongg.
DISPLAY and XAUTHORITY are inherited from the desktop.

This is a native T800 C++ build, including GIF decoding, using the LLVM
Helios C++ runtime and rebuilt X11R4 Xlib. The port uses the shared C++-compatible R4 headers and Helios's select descriptor
representation, and includes errno.h directly.

The source bundle, documentation and build recipe accompany the installed
port. Upstream copyright and licence notices remain in the source.
